# Explorable: the picture answers to the user's hand with no round trip.
# A slider scrubs, a toggle switches, a pick changes the picture's mood, and a
# button asks the brain for what it cannot know.

scene figure lines=3
line ground 10,78 150,78 thick=1
rect post 30,48 3x30 fill=ink
line shadow 33,78 120,78 stroke=accent thick=2
circle sun 30,14 6 fill=accent soft=3
path sky stroke=none | M30 14 Q90 6 140 60
card tools | Try it
slider height 10 80 20 unit=deg in=tools | Height of the sun
toggle shade on in=tools | Show the shadow
pick view tabs in=tools | Day | Dusk | Night
bind height | move sun along=sky
bind height | line shadow 33,78 38,78
bind shade=off | set shadow opacity=0
bind view=dusk | set sun fill=#ff8a4c
bind view=night | set sun fill=dim
say | At {height} degrees a 3 m post throws a shadow {round(3/tan(rad(height)), 1)} m long.
button ask | Why is it longer at dusk?
